{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-16T09:19:22.579Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0f2e9ab0717c8648158fe950","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-16T09:19:22.579Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Three valid traced 100-subscriber runs: p50/p95/p99/max ms 198.5/485.5/633.9/633.9; 308.2/1492.4/2965.8/2965.8; 245.0/956.1/1239.2/1239.2. All 50/50 writes committed; zero loss/duplicates. Breach reproduced in trace run 2: CLI timestamp-to-history-append p99 2247.5 ms, including index-file-lock acquisition lower bound p99 2071.0 ms; detecting read/classification p99 1106.7 ms; polling wait p99 232.4 ms. Shared serialization p99 HTTP/CLI 1.45/9.50 ms; client write p99 0.048/0.025 ms. The pinned SDK serializes history-index readers and appenders on an exclusive index-file lock before authoritative history append. No safe pm-web hot-path repair is justified by this evidence; preserve replay/dedupe/authorization unchanged, draft upstream issue here without filing it. Stop expansion at 100 after SLO breach; 250/500/1000 remain unmeasured. Three earlier full traces and two small diagnostic runs were inconclusive while validating probes and are excluded. Raw reports remain external; public-safe summary and methods will be committed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-16T09:19:22.579Z"}],"before_hash":"ddbf0c8692789bfeddd057e07be70f816145dda16a5b932c27649b0d4de120d1","after_hash":"bd7f09f84678a26ec0088c16ddf7f0da215ebc0ce7e4c4fa0eaaa4f42ecc3996","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"co