{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-16T09:22:04.470Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0f2e9ab0717c8648158fe950","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-16T09:22:04.470Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"DRAFT UPSTREAM ISSUE (not filed). Title: Mixed history-index readers and writers can delay authoritative append beyond a 2-second delivery budget. Package: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.15. Reproduce with the public pm-web capacity harness, disposable test Postgres, 100 authenticated SSE readers, five HTTP SDK writer lanes and five separate pinned CLI writer lanes, five independent item updates each; retain ordinary 250 ms mutation polling and 60-second inclusive replay. docs/capacity/2026-10-16-local.md records three untraced p99 values 1181.3/898.9/913.2 ms and three traced values 633.9/2965.8/1239.2 ms. In the breached run, all 50 updates and 5000 receipts arrived exactly once. CLI timestamp-to-authoritative-append p99/max 2247.5 ms independently exceeds the total 2000 ms SLO; index-file-lock wait lower bound p99/max is 2071.0 ms. Detecting SDK read/classification p99 1106.7 ms, polling wait p99 232.4 ms; per-client write p99 under 0.05 ms. Implementation inspection: queryHistoryEventIndex and appendHistoryEntryWithEventIndex both acquire withHistoryEventIndexLock; append acquires before authoritative history write and queries validate stream sizes under that exclusive lock. Expected: committed-fact readers should not introduce unbounded writer latency or visibility loss. Investigate a validated nonblocking/read snapshot strategy or fair lock acquisition while preserving authoritative fallback and late-fact visibility; do not remove validation or timestamp overlap blindly. Clock starts before persistence by harness contract, not at fsync or response. Shared-host scheduling and probe perturbation remain confounders; reader-versus-writer contention contribution and the original busy-host breach are not separately proven. No upstream mutation or filing performed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-16T09:22:04.470Z"}],"before_hash":"9355062299dc14450c9a8c23422475a6c11cee5a8bcedcd0e3816169095ac301","after_hash":"a0718de4059fcf706ef044103509ec3f20bd80655bfa70fd894627c63828fa06","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"39a41549ea7864c807500e9049b74ad057bddcaf95f661abe913cefd85883109"}
